{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-100720",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The denominators are $5$ and $4.$ We can make a common denominator of $5\\times 4=20.$ \n\nWe split the shape on the left of the division sign into $4$ parts vertically, and we split the shape on the right into $5$ parts horizontally:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14155061/assets/d456f6fe7acc94b5a9e8e366fb2faea3ec2683e731a5e4cdafcdcbf6ce685bd2.png)\n\nSo, our division problem now is\n\n$$\n\\frac{12}{20}÷\\frac{15}{20}.\n$$\n\nSince the denominators are equal, this is equivalent to\n\n$$\n12÷15=\\frac{12}{15}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}÷\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{12}{15}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
